# The engine repo holds only the engine and the basics a local run and the
# licence need. Everything else on this machine is local-only: notes, agent
# instructions, tool state, and the operator's private folders. None of it is
# ever committed here.
#
# This is a whitelist, not a list of things to ignore. Ignore every top-level
# entry, then re-include the engine and its basics. A new top-level file or
# folder is ignored until it is named here on purpose, so nothing internal can
# be swept in by a broad `git add`.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/.ignore
!/LICENSE.txt
!/README.md
!/llms.txt
!/install.sh
!/mcp/
!/public/
!/shared/
!/skills/

# Secrets are never committed, even inside a re-included path.
*.pem
*.key
credentials*.json
secrets*.json
.env
.env.*
